From: Mocha bring-up <mocha@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rt5670: guard optional jack GPIO cleanup

Speaker-only cards do not call rt5670_set_jack_detect(). Their jack pointer
and GPIO delayed work are uninitialized. Unconditionally freeing them on
card removal causes a workqueue warning and a NULL dereference.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/rt5670.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/rt5670.c
@@ -2755,7 +2755,8 @@ static void rt5670_remove(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 	struct rt5670_priv *rt5670 = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(component);
 
 	regmap_write(rt5670->regmap, RT5670_RESET, 0);
-	snd_soc_jack_free_gpios(rt5670->jack, 1, &rt5670->hp_gpio);
+	if (rt5670->jack)
+		snd_soc_jack_free_gpios(rt5670->jack, 1, &rt5670->hp_gpio);
 }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM
